      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that the arithmetic mean of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) is 18, we can write:\n\\[\n\\frac{x + y}{2} = 18\n\\]\nMultiplying both sides by 2, we get:\n\\[\nx + y = 36\n\\]\n\nGiven that the geometric mean of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) is \\(\\sqrt{92}\\), we can write:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{xy} = \\sqrt{92}\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\\[\nxy = 92\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(x^2 + y^2\\). We can use the identity:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = (x + y)^2 - 2xy\n\\]\nSubstituting the values we have:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = 36^2 - 2 \\cdot 92\n\\]\nCalculating the squares and the product:\n\\[\n36^2 = 1296\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 92 = 184\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 = 1296 - 184 = 1112\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(x^2 + y^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{1112}\\).",
